  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data:** The `kibana_sample_data_logs` index has three response codes: 200 (12,832 requests), 404 (801), and 503 (441). The top countries by request count are CN, IN, and US. The data's timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-442b0759 Web logs overview\"** has four panels:\n- **Total requests:** a single-number count of all requests.\n- **5xx responses (503):** a single-number count filtered to `response.keyword: 503`.\n- **Requests over time by response code:** a line chart over `timestamp`, split by response code.\n- **Top countries by requests (geo.dest):** a bar chart of the top 10 countries.\n\nI set the dashboard's time range to October 1 through December 31, 2026, so the sample data shows up. Today is 2026-10-12, so the default last-7-days range would have shown little.\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-442b0759 5xx spike\"** (ID `6b8cd94e-ffa0-49e1-8a69-5b18154adb16`):\n- Type `.es-query` in the `stackAlerts` consumer, checking every 1m.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` in the last 5 minutes, with `timestamp` as the time field.\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- Enabled.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- The 5xx rule uses a wildcard (`5*`), not `503` alone, so any future 5xx codes are counted too.\n- The 5xx panel filters on `503` alone because it is the only 5xx code in the data.\n\nThe sample data is dated in the future relative to today, so the rule's 5-minute window will likely see no matches until the sample data's timestamps fall within the window. I didn't confirm the rule's first run.",
